-- title:
--   Characteristic 2 supersingular lift with distinguished j-polynomial
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=2$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $q$ and let $E_0$ be a Weierstrass curve over $k$ with invertible discriminant whose formal group is supersingular in the sense that, for the ideal $\bot$ of $k$, $(0,0)$ is a Drinfeld basis of level $q$: the $q$-th multiplication series $[q]$ of $E_0$'s formal group is a unit of $k\llbracket X\rrbracket$ times the Drinfeld divisor attached to $q,0,0$ (equivalently, by the cited criterion, a unit times $X^{q^2}$). Let $W_0$ be a complete discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by $q$, together with a surjective ring map $\mathrm{res}_0 : W_0 \to k$ whose kernel is that maximal ideal. The assertion is the existence of: a Weierstrass curve $\mathcal E$ over $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$ with $\Delta(\mathcal E)$ a unit, whose base change along $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ (t \mapsto 0)$ is $E_0$; a commutative formal group $F_u$ over $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$ whose two-variable series is the Weierstrass formal group law `formalGroupLawFixed` of $\mathcal E$ and whose image under $\mathrm{res}_0 \circ (t\mapsto 0)$ is the formal group of $E_0$; such that the coefficient $\gamma$ of $Z^q$ in the $q$-th multiplication series of $F_u$ has $t$-linear coefficient congruent to $1$ modulo the maximal ideal of $W_0$ and satisfies $\gamma \equiv u_1 t$ modulo $q\,W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$ for some unit $u_1$; and, finally, an element $a_0 \in W_0$, an integer $e \ge 1$, a unit $u_2$ of $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$ and a monic $P \in W_0[X]$ of degree $e$ with $P_i$ in the $\big((e-i)q/(q+1) + 1\big)$-th power of the maximal ideal for all $i < e$ (natural-number division), for which $j(\mathcal E) - a_0 = u_2 \cdot P(t)$ in $W_0\llbracket t\rrbracket$, where $j(\mathcal E)$ is computed from the invertibility of $\Delta(\mathcal E)$.
--
--   This is the characteristic-$2$ case of the construction of an explicit one-parameter lift of a supersingular elliptic curve in which the Hasse parameter serves as the deformation coordinate (Igusa's simple zero of the Hasse invariant), with the $j$-invariant expressed as a unit times a distinguished Weierstrass polynomial whose roots lie deeper than the Drinfeld depth $q/(q+1)$. It is used by [`WeierstrassCurve.exists_powerSeries_lift_coeff_nthSeries_sub_mul_X_mem_span_and_jOfUnit_sub_eq_mul_eval`](thm.html#WeierstrassCurve.exists_powerSeries_lift_coeff_nthSeries_sub_mul_X_mem_span_and_jOfUnit_sub_eq_mul_eval), the statement uniform in the residue characteristic.
